# Skill: UI Component Builder

## When to use
When creating or modifying React components that have visual output.

## Instructions
1. Read design-system.md before writing any CSS
2. Use Tailwind utility classes, not custom CSS
3. Create a mobile-first layout (start with mobile, add breakpoints for larger screens)
4. Every component needs: a loading state, an error state, and an empty state
5. After building, take a screenshot and evaluate against the design system

## Quality checks
- Contrast ratio meets WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text)
- Touch targets are at least 44x44px on mobile
- No hardcoded colors (use design system tokens)
